ranch must be additive, not reordering this one\\\" |\\n| 13 | GraphQL path scope decision: explicitly documented as out of scope; any future x-ratelimit-reset fallback there is a separate decision | AVAILABLE | Impact Radius Unknown frontier section: states \\\"confirm whether the GraphQL path is in or out of scope before closing\\\" with note on current behavior (Retry-After only, no fallback) |\\n| 14 | Live rate-limit response carries x-ratelimit-reset reliably across deployment environments | AVAILABLE | Impact Radius Unknown frontier: cites PyGithub's Requester.createException passes raw headers unmodified; closure path: live e2e rate-limit test lane or captured real response |\\n\\n**Counts**: AVAILABLE 14, DERIVABLE 0, MISSING 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\n**Changes from snapshot**:\\n- Initial assessment by orchestrator contained no prior RT-ICA section; this is the first assessment.\\n- All 14 conditions evaluated to AVAILABLE based on Fact-Check verification, Root-Cause Analysis, and Impact Radius Systems Inventory completeness.\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T23:19:10.023886Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: Primary-quota 403 rate limit is classified non-retryable\\nDate: 2026-09-28\\nGoal: A primary-quota 403 (RateLimitExceededException / exhausted x-ratelimit-remaining) classifies as RETRYABLE with a delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After is absent.\\nConditions:\\n1. Location of the misclassification (sync_state._classify_github_exception, 403 branch) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: sync_state.py:352-379 read in session; Fact-Check entry 1 claim 1 VERIFIED\\n2. Existing rate-limit detector and import-direction constraint (gh_client._is_rate_limited; gh_client imports sync_state, not the reverse) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: gh_client.py:892-916; sync_state.py _github_exception_message_text docstring states the import direction\\n3. How the delay flows from classifier to sync backoff and MCP retryable/retry_after | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check entry 2 claim 2 VERIFIED (sync_engine._attempt_sync, server._failure_verdict call retry_after_seconds and _retryable)\\n4. Shape of GitHub primary-limit responses | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check entry 2 claim 1 VERIFIED against GitHub REST docs: x-ratelimit-remaining: 0 and x-ratelimit-reset (epoch s), no Retry-After\\n5. (new) GraphQL rate-limit delay path lacks the x-ratelimit-reset fallback | Snapshot: \u2014 \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check entry 2 claim 3 VERIFIED (GitHubRateLimitedError delay from parse_retry_after_header only)\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker, claim 2)\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker, claim 1)\\n- Condition 5: (new) AVAILABLE \u2014 discovered by impact-analyst Unknown Frontier, verified by fact-checker claim 3. [AUTO] Brought into scope (the rtica-assessor had marked it out-of-scope): the item's goal is a delay from x-ratelimit-reset whenever Retry-After is absent, and the GraphQL path fails the same goal. Acceptance Criterion 9 records it.\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T22:07:05.787449Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Traceable failure with identifiable cause chain. RateLimitExceededException (temporary GitHub primary-quota 403) is misclassified as non-retryable due to generic 403 rule executing before exception-type-specific check. Reproduction: primary rate limit exhaustion during sync. Fix location is known (sync_state._classify_github_exception).\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Primary GitHub rate limit (temporary, always resolves in 60 seconds) incorrectly pauses sync as if it were a permanent auth error \u2192 Primary rate limit is recognized as retryable with correct delay extracted from x-ratelimit-reset header\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T23:09:50.193475Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-28T09:49:52.040545Z \u2014 Added file/line evidence for the three scope-added issues (A, B, C), each verified directly against source on 2026-09-28. Also corrected the `test_sync_state_classify.py` path, which was listed under `backlog_core/tests/` but was confirmed via `ls` to live at `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sync_state_classify.py` \u2014 the `backlog_core/tests/` path does not exist.</summary>\\n\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_state.py \u2014 `_classify_github_exception` (403 branch, ~lines 351-378); `retry_after_seconds` / `parse_retry_after_header` (~lines 412-460); classification-table docstring (~lines 504-540)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_engine.py \u2014 `_attempt_sync` (~lines 196-221, 257-260), consumer\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py \u2014 `_retryable`, `_failure_verdict` (~lines 260-323), consumer\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py \u2014 `_is_rate_limited` (~lines 892-916, already correct, not touched); `_graphql_request` (~lines 964-974) and issue-status-map builder (~line 2291), consumers with an open GraphQL-scope question (see Blockers on the item's Impact Radius)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py \u2014 `fetch_snapshot`, `fetch_page`, `search_issues_by_title`, `fetch_issue_titles`, `confirm_issues_reachable` (~lines 294-556), consumers\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_retryable_classification.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_rate_limit_retry_after.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sync_state_secondary_rate_limit.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_startup_sync.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sync_state_graphql_refu