n- [x] Tests, docs, config, CI, operations, and agent instructions checked\\n- [x] Applicable data, model, prompt, context, people, process, and control effects checked\\n- [x] Transition, rollback, delayed effects, and observability checked\\n- [x] Replacement or removal preserves the purpose of existing capabilities and controls\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-28T11:06:17.058454Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: Found 2 systems outside the starting impact set - the MCP tool retry-verdict contract and the multi-call-site GitHub backend consumers that all route through the same classifier. This expands fact-check scope to: `backlog_core/server.py::_retryable`/`_failure_verdict` (MCP `retryable`/`retry_after` response fields), `backlog_core/sync_engine.py::_attempt_sync` (background sync retry/backoff), `backlog_core/gh_client.py` (2 call sites), `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py` (6 call sites).\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION (2026-09-28 amendment): Found 3 more systems approved by the repo owner - `backlog_core/gh_client.py::probe_backend_status` (Issue A, reuses the same classifier instead of its own any-403-is-rate-limited rule), `backlog_core/github_client.py::make_github_client`/`_BoundedGithubRetry` (Issue B, bounds PyGithub's in-transport rate-limit sleep), and `backlog_core/parsing.py::view_result_from_local_item`/`_coerce_issue_number` (Issue C, unrelated `backlog_view` `number: null` defect) - plus 2 orchestrator-added systems: `backlog_core/sync_state.py::RETRYABLE_TRANSIENT_EXCEPTIONS` (classify `requests.exceptions.RetryError` retryable) and `backlog_core/models.py::ViewItemResultCompact` (delete, zero live references), plus a stale-claim correction in `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and three new/extended test files (`tests/test_backend_status.py`, `backlog_core/tests/test_github_client.py`, `tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py`).\\nIMPACT_RADIUS_COMPLETE: Written to item #3978. Overall risk: MEDIUM. Highest-risk: backlog_core/sync_state.py (classifier + retry-delay source of truth); backlog_core/sync_engine.py (retry/backoff timing); backlog_core/github_client.py::_BoundedGithubRetry (process-wide REST retry-transport change, Issue B).\\n\\n### Change Frame\\n- Baseline: `sync_state._classify_github_exception`'s 403 branch treats any REST 403 as retryable only when it carries a `Retry-After` header or a \\\"secondary rate limit\\\" message substring. A primary-quota 403 (`RateLimitExceededException`, \\\"API rate limit exceeded\\\", typically no `Retry-After`) falls through to NON_RETRYABLE. `retry_after_seconds` only reads the `Retry-After` header/GraphQL `retry_after`; it has no fallback to `x-ratelimit-reset`.\\n- Delta: classify `RateLimitExceededException` (or an equivalent primary-limit signal) as RETRYABLE ahead of the generic 403 rule, and derive a retry delay from the `x-ratelimit-reset` header (an epoch timestamp requiring a `reset - now` conversion) when `Retry-After` is absent.\\n- Intended outcome: a primary-quota 403 keeps the background sync retrying (with a delay long enough not to hit the same limit again) instead of parking in OFFLINE, and MCP tool error responses report `retryable: true` with a `retry_after` hint for the same failure.\\n- Non-goals: the GraphQL rate-limit path (`gh_client._graphql_request`'s `GitHubRateLimitedError` construction), the secondary-rate-limit branch, and `gh_client.probe_backend_status`'s independent 403-handling are not named by the item and are called out separately below.\\n- Time horizon and rollback boundary: pure classification/delay-computation logic, no schema or stored-state migration; revertible by reverting the diff. The only carried state is in-memory `SyncState` (process singleton), so no persisted data needs backfill.\\n\\n### Impact Pathways\\n- `RateLimitExceededException raised -> _classify_github_exception 403 branch -> SyncErrorKind flips NON_RETRYABLE to RETRYABLE -> classify_sync_error -> sync_engine._attempt_sync keeps retrying instead of setting OFFLINE` | Owner: background sync loop | Evidence: backlog_core/sync_engine.py:205-221 | Confidence: OBSERVED | Verification: unit test asserting `classify_sync_error(RateLimitExceededException(...))` is RETRYABLE and `_attempt_sync` does not set `SyncStatus.OFFLINE` for it.\\n- `retry_after_seconds gains an x-ratelimit-reset fallback -> state.retry_after computed from GitHub's reset time -> sync_engine's backoff delay (max(backoff, retry_after)) can be much larger than the fixed exponential schedule` | Owner: background sync loop | Evidence: backlog_core/sync_engine.py:257-260 | Confidence: OBSERVED | Verification: test that a far-future `x-ratelimit-reset` produces a bounded, non-negative delay and does not stall the event loop or exceed `MAX_RETRIES` prematurely.\\n- `classify_github_failure's verdict flips -> server._retryable / _failure_verdict -> MCP tool error payloads (backlog_list, backlog_view, sync_now, etc.) report retryable: true + retry_after where they previously reported false with no hint` | Owner: MCP tool callers (agents) | Evidence: backlog_core/server.py:260-323 | Confidence: OBSERVED | Verification: `tests/test_retryable_classification.py`-style parametrized case for a primary-limit `RateLimitExceededException` with no `Retry-After`.\\n- `classify_sync_error/classify_github_failure verdict flips -> backends/github_backend.py (fetch_snapshot, fetch_page, search_issues_by_title, fetch_issue_titles, confirm_issues_reachable) and gh_client.py (_graphql_request's non-rate-limited branch, issue-status-map builder) recompute BackendUnavailableError.retryable` | Owner: GitHub backend read/write paths | Evidence: backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py:294-556; backlog_core/gh_client.py:965-974,2288-2292 | Confidence: OBSERVED | Verification: existing parametrized suites in these files re-run with a `RateLimitExceededException` fixture added.\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n- `backlog_core/sync_state.py::_classify_github_exception` - primary edit site